{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-69726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})=[]+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $5$ and position $3$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}) &  & (\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3})=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2})+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{3})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6e17cf9063e7e4fb3415570f105ee6703f54bb19f94d3653d5120bc5c0d6a146"} {"question" "q-69726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{1}{0})"] ["math" "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{2}{1})"] ["math" "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{2})"] ["math" "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{3}{3})"] ["math" "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=4$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}) & =\\frac{4!}{(4-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2!}{2!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6e17cf9063e7e4fb3415570f105ee6703f54bb19f94d3653d5120bc5c0d6a146"} {"question" "q-69994" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69994" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69994" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=6$ and $r=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}) & =\\frac{6!}{(6-3)!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3!}{3!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{6}\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{\\cancel{3\\cdot 2}\\cdot \\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6e17cf9063e7e4fb3415570f105ee6703f54bb19f94d3653d5120bc5c0d6a146"} {"question" "q-69995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-69995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-70306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-70306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=5$ and $r=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{3}) & =\\frac{5!}{(5-3)!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3!}{2!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4\\cdot \\cancel{3!}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{3!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{2} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042747/state.json" "file_sha256" "37f01f51d789dc285a53f9110c26287ae40af8c0edb6d6af8a460d8f1f40e6f3"} {"question" "q-70306" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma